1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,830
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:10,540
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,440
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,250
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:21,480
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:40,870
Guts!

7
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:41,910
Take up that sword!

8
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:27,520
Feel no shame about shape

9
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:29,440
Weather changes their phrase

10
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:33,190
Even mother will show you another way

11
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:35,570
So put your glasses on

12
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:37,660
Nothing will be wrong

13
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:39,870
There's no blame. There's no fame

14
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:41,700
It's up to you

15
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:45,330
The first words should be found

16
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,960
Whatever holds you back

17
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:50,330
I...

18
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:51,460
...can...

19
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:53,630
I can get it off

20
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:54,630
Tell me what...

21
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:55,630
Tell me what...

22
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,470
Tell me what you want

23
00:01:57,590 --> 00:01:58,550
I don't know why...

24
00:01:58,760 --> 00:01:59,550
Don't know why...

25
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:01,550
Don't know why you're afraid

26
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:02,720
Tell me what...

27
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:03,680
Tell me what...

28
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:05,350
Tell me what you'd say

29
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:06,680
I don't know why...

30
00:02:06,810 --> 00:02:07,770
Don't know why...

31
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:08,560
Too late...

32
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:10,190
It's too late

33
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:19,110
Moment of Glory

34
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,920
Griffith!

35
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:44,220
Wow!

36
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:46,390
I didn't know that so many
people lived in Windham!

37
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:04,700
Pippin!

38
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:11,500
Miss Casca!

39
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,830
My dear sister, please turn around!

40
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,380
I can't take it...

41
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:17,800
The Raiders!

42
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:20,090
Commander Guts is taking the lead!

43
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:23,720
He is the man who defeated General Boscone!

44
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:26,310
The Band of the Hawk's strongest warrior!

45
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:28,970
This is great!

46
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:32,850
I've never seen such
an enthusiastic victory parade before.

47
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:36,650
Well, why don't you wave your
arm or something, Commander?

48
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:39,650
You are the hero of the battle, after all.

49
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:41,650
Commander?

50
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,660
What's the matter?

51
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:47,160
You look a little down.

52
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:49,080
Really, I'm okay...

53
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:51,460
It's real...

54
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:56,340
Could anyone have even dreamt
of this day three years ago?

55
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,880
That's true!

56
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,010
But one man did...

57
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:01,880
Only him...

58
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:06,800
I will have my own kingdom...

59
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:09,970
It's amazing...

60
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:11,350
Really...

61
00:04:16,650 --> 00:04:18,440
There he is, my lady!

62
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:22,070
Look, Sir Griffith is so popular!

63
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:24,280
All of the women are in a frenzy.

64
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,620
How dare they get so close to him!

65
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:27,320
Acting so forward!

66
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:29,240
Please, make haste!

67
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,330
My lady, please stand still, will you?

68
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:33,750
Otherwise, your dress...

69
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,830
Tell me, how do I look?

70
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:38,170
You look fantastic in it.

71
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:42,920
You have changed into five dresses,
my lady. It's best to decide now.

72
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,550
Really?

73
00:04:44,930 --> 00:04:46,390
But I think...

74
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:48,600
My lady, come here and hurry!

75
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,510
He is passing by, hurry!

76
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:52,350
Wait, wait!

77
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:56,520
The princess sure became
cheerful all of a sudden.

78
00:04:56,940 --> 00:05:01,610
She would barely eat when
the Band of the Hawk was in the field.

79
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:09,910
Sir Griffith!

80
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:16,210
Oh no!

81
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:19,380
It is impossible in this noisy crowd.

82
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,340
You had best wait until the celebration.

83
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:31,810
Did you make the arrangements?

84
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:33,680
Consider it done.

85
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:39,980
We should hold a feast to celebrate
after everything has fallen into place.

86
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:43,070
A feast held to express
our regrets over his death.

87
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,320
How ironic.

88
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:49,990
The battlefield's White Hawk will meet
his end in a birdcage of stone walls.

89
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:55,250
Of course, it will happen on this day,
the most notable in his entire life.

90
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:57,960
This is merciful, at least.

91
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,710
Minister Foss!

92
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,920
What's happened?

93
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,460
I've brought a letter addressed to you, sir.

94
00:06:05,550 --> 00:06:06,760
A letter?

95
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,260
But from who?

96
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,640
I do not know.

97
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,760
A lady from the court entrusted this to me.

98
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,390
Excuse me.

99
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:21,150
T-This is...

100
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:23,150
What is the matter, Minister Foss?

101
00:06:24,610 --> 00:06:26,110
W-Well...

102
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,990
Nothing is the matter, Your Majesty.

103
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:37,160
I have a little errand to take
care of, so please excuse me.

104
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,660
See you later then.

105
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,800
How?

106
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:52,010
How did this happen?

107
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,930
Bastard!

108
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:27,920
Look!

109
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:30,340
Here comes Sir Griffith!

110
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,380
The Band of the Hawk's members?

111
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:34,010
Midland's guardian angels!

112
00:07:45,730 --> 00:07:46,770
I see.

113
00:07:47,150 --> 00:07:50,690
The heavy taxes on
the commoners is spent on this place.

114
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:51,360
Yeah...

115
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:55,780
Hey, stick out your chest!

116
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:58,080
They will look down on you
if you aren't confident!

117
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:01,120
I'm so nervous. It's embarrassing.

118
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:05,540
But we have come this far at last.

119
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,540
That's true.

120
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:12,010
I can't believe I'm standing in a place
I've only heard about in fairy tales!

121
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:17,470
If I hadn't met the Band
of the Hawk and Griffith...

122
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:22,560
...I would never have even imagined
this sight, not even in a dream...

123
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:25,520
Me, surrounded by nobles
in a huge castle like this.

124
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:32,650
Sir Griffith!

125
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,280
Welcome back, my lord.

126
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:37,820
Pleased to see you safe.
We were worried about you.

127
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:42,330
I heard that you all carried
the battle on your shoulders again.

128
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:44,870
Please tell us your stories of the battlefield.

129
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:47,880
Would you mind
if I offered myself for a dance later?

130
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:50,210
I would love to dance with you too!

131
00:08:50,210 --> 00:08:51,340
No, tell us your story first.

132
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:57,260
I am afraid of boring you ladies
by telling a barbarous war tale.

133
00:08:57,260 --> 00:09:01,390
We wouldn't be bored at all.
It's very exciting!

134
00:09:01,390 --> 00:09:02,390
Yes!

135
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:04,890
Wow...

136
00:09:04,890 --> 00:09:06,600
He certainly seems at home...

137
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:11,440
Damn, he should share
one of them with me!

138
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,440
You must be the Band of
the Hawk's commanders?

139
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:16,610
I would like you to tell me your
heroic exploits on the battlefield.

140
00:09:16,610 --> 00:09:19,410
You certainly are strong, aren't you?

141
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:23,250
Well, I really am I must confess.

142
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:25,580
I am even afraid of my own strength.

143
00:09:26,250 --> 00:09:28,000
It's you, isn't it?

144
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:32,130
The raider commander who defeated
General Boscone in single combat?

145
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,460
Y-Yeah...

146
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:35,880
How fabulous!

147
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,260
Despite the fact that General Boscone...

148
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:41,010
...was their great hero, and every
country knows his reputation.

149
00:09:41,010 --> 00:09:41,850
That's true!

150
00:09:41,850 --> 00:09:46,480
I also heard that you defeated
a hundred men all by yourself.

151
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,850
Is that true?

152
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:49,770
Y-Yeah...

153
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:51,570
This is unbelievable!

154
00:09:51,570 --> 00:09:54,440
Are you the strongest
in the Band of the Hawk?

155
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:57,150
Who is stronger, Sir Griffith or you?

156
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:01,410
Hey, you take care of them!

157
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:02,490
Oh no!

158
00:10:02,490 --> 00:10:03,870
He's leaving!

159
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:05,620
All right, no problem!

160
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,830
No fair, Guts!

161
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:10,000
So cute!

162
00:10:10,330 --> 00:10:11,340
Um...

163
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,790
How muscular!

164
00:10:12,790 --> 00:10:14,710
Let me touch! Let me touch!

165
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,260
Look how carried away they are...

166
00:10:23,810 --> 00:10:27,020
Deep down, all of them probably
feel undeserving of this praise.

167
00:10:27,020 --> 00:10:28,810
Perhaps...

168
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:35,230
But even the generals must recognize
the Band of the Hawk's true strength.

169
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:36,610
Of course.

170
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:39,240
Because one hundred years later...

171
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:42,120
...they have fulfilled our
kingdom's long-cherished wish.

172
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,370
As if it were nothing.

173
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:47,830
It was wise that you spoke up
for him earlier, Sir Raban.

174
00:10:48,210 --> 00:10:50,540
You have foresight,
and I will follow your example.

175
00:10:50,870 --> 00:10:54,670
You're starting to sound like a certain
minister we all know, Sir Owen.

176
00:10:55,460 --> 00:11:00,130
However, we will all need
to be a little like that in future.

177
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,260
The war is over.

178
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:08,310
I pray to God that the upcoming
peace and tranquility will last for ages...

179
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:15,020
In a period of peace, warriors like us
who only know how to wield swords...

180
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:18,530
...have to find a new way
to survive within the castle.

181
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:24,910
Ironically, the man who brought this
peace must also be aware of this...

182
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:30,500
That man stands out too much
to be a part of the court...

183
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,130
...without causing a disturbance.

184
00:11:33,790 --> 00:11:36,290
The stronger a light shines...

185
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,340
...the darker the nearby shadows grow.

186
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:50,980
Oh, jeez...

187
00:11:51,350 --> 00:11:52,890
I can't deal with this.

188
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:54,520
What are they doing?

189
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,120
Come on!

190
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,410
H-Hey, wait...

191
00:12:10,410 --> 00:12:11,040
What the...

192
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:12,330
Who the hell are you?

193
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:16,790
Those men are pestering me,
and I don't know what to do.

194
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:19,420
I want you to pretend that
you're my partner for a while.

195
00:12:21,090 --> 00:12:22,590
It's annoying!

196
00:12:22,590 --> 00:12:26,760
Those useless sons of noblemen
must not see many female warriors.

197
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:29,060
They look at me like
I'm some kind of rare animal...

198
00:12:33,730 --> 00:12:35,230
What are you looking at?

199
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:37,230
I didn't know you liked to wear...

200
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,820
Don't tell me that...

201
00:12:43,950 --> 00:12:45,110
Just come this way!

202
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:47,740
How embarrassing!

203
00:12:48,530 --> 00:12:49,790
It's not my fault!

204
00:12:54,790 --> 00:12:56,580
I see...

205
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:01,340
I'm not very good at these kinds of things.

206
00:13:02,010 --> 00:13:05,300
Wielding a sword is much more comfortable.

207
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:06,340
I agree.

208
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:08,970
But I wonder what put
such an idea into your head?

209
00:13:08,970 --> 00:13:13,480
To think that you, our brave sister
Casca, is wearing a flowing dress...

210
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:16,730
I normally dress like a man simply
because it's easier to move that way.

211
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:19,270
It doesn't mean that
I'm fond of wearing men's clothes!

212
00:13:21,570 --> 00:13:22,480
But...

213
00:13:23,530 --> 00:13:25,780
I shouldn't have done
something I'm not used to.

214
00:13:26,150 --> 00:13:29,870
I'll make myself sick if I keep
wearing these kinds of loose dresses.

215
00:13:30,530 --> 00:13:35,160
Come to think of it,
I haven't worn a skirt for so long...

216
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,370
And look at all my muscles...

217
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:40,340
Don't I look ridiculous?

218
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:42,630
No, you look good.

219
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:43,800
Really?

220
00:13:44,170 --> 00:13:50,350
Sure, you look better than
the noble girls crowding around Griffith.

221
00:13:54,430 --> 00:13:58,310
Hey, why don't you ask
Griffith to dance with you?

222
00:13:58,940 --> 00:13:59,860
No...

223
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:02,020
It's impossible...

224
00:14:02,770 --> 00:14:06,610
I haven't danced since those small
village festivals when I was a kid.

225
00:14:07,070 --> 00:14:09,530
I'd end up stepping on Griffith's feet...

226
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:16,960
Anyway, tell me why you've
had such a change of heart.

227
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:21,590
You've never showed up
in stuffy places like this before...

228
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,220
I want to see everything
through to the end...

229
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:28,760
What?

230
00:14:29,470 --> 00:14:32,010
Ever since I met you three years ago...

231
00:14:32,470 --> 00:14:34,100
...what Griffith and I...

232
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,520
What everyone has done within these years...

233
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:44,980
...and what he has won so far,
and what he will win in the future...

234
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:47,940
I want to see it to the end.

235
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,110
That's why I came.

236
00:14:55,330 --> 00:14:56,370
Guts...

237
00:14:57,660 --> 00:15:01,120
So you do want to...
the Band of the Hawk.

238
00:15:03,790 --> 00:15:05,050
For real?

239
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:11,010
No matter what?

240
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,980
Long live the king!

241
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:20,270
Long live the king!

242
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:28,320
His Majesty has arrived.

243
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,280
You go on ahead.

244
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:35,240
I'll stay here and cool off for a while.

245
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:39,750
I can't stand listening to
the king's tedious speeches.

246
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:40,960
Don't be too long.

247
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:41,500
Sure...

248
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:44,750
You...

249
00:15:45,210 --> 00:15:45,840
What?

250
00:15:47,170 --> 00:15:47,960
No...

251
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:50,470
Nothing...

252
00:16:01,310 --> 00:16:05,440
There is another reason why
I'm here at this evening party.

253
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:09,820
No one knows what will
happen here in a few moments.

254
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:12,900
Not Casca or the other
Band of the Hawk guys...

255
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:18,120
It's a little too much
for them, isn't it, Griffith?

256
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:24,500
First of all, I shall share
some good news with you.

257
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:31,010
A little while ago, Tudor envoys
were sent to our kingdom.

258
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:34,430
They carried a signed armistice treaty.

259
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:40,180
I am most grateful for your strength and
fortitude through these horrible times.

260
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:43,060
I should like to express my utmost gratitude.

261
00:16:43,850 --> 00:16:48,820
It is understandable that more than
a few of you might be displeased...

262
00:16:49,230 --> 00:16:50,480
...by the armistice.

263
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:53,610
After all, many of you have lost
your family and friends to this war...

264
00:16:53,610 --> 00:16:58,740
...and our enmity toward Tudor
has been harbored for generations.

265
00:16:59,030 --> 00:17:03,910
However, it is urgent for us
to rebuild our kingdom.

266
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:07,670
Our kingdom has been
exhausted due to the war effort.

267
00:17:07,670 --> 00:17:13,420
I expect everyone to contribute all they
can to return our land to prosperity.

268
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,180
As you well know...

269
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:23,730
...this armistice is due to the Band of
the Hawk's merits, led by Count Griffith.

270
00:17:23,730 --> 00:17:25,850
Due to their distinguished service.

271
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:27,810
During the past one hundred years...

272
00:17:27,810 --> 00:17:31,440
...it has been said the conquest of
Doldrey would be utterly impossible.

273
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:38,070
But they succeeded with unparalleled
courage in such an undertaking.

274
00:17:38,070 --> 00:17:40,530
Excuse me, let me pass please.

275
00:17:40,870 --> 00:17:46,410
And I will inform you now, at this
joyous celebration, that there will be...

276
00:17:46,410 --> 00:17:49,750
...a rite of decoration
held the day after tomorrow...

277
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:55,050
I deem it proper to confer upon Count
Griffith and the Band of the Hawk...

278
00:17:55,050 --> 00:18:00,550
...the title of White Knights and
highest authority over Midland's army.

279
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,930
Their official titles will most likely be...

280
00:18:03,930 --> 00:18:08,100
...White Hawk General Griffith
and the White Hawk Knights.

281
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:11,730
All of the Band of the Hawk's
company commanders...

282
00:18:12,070 --> 00:18:17,570
...will be personally knighted
by myself and raised to the peerage.

283
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:19,820
The White Hawk General!

284
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,570
The White Hawk Knights!

285
00:18:21,910 --> 00:18:22,950
Wonderful!

286
00:18:22,950 --> 00:18:24,040
So amazing!

287
00:18:32,090 --> 00:18:34,210
I can't believe this...

288
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,760
We're going to become noblemen! Us!

289
00:18:56,190 --> 00:18:58,110
Isn't it wonderful?

290
00:18:58,110 --> 00:18:59,490
Uh, thank you...

291
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,490
Please let me pass.

292
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,210
Why...

293
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:12,460
A commoner, promoted
to the highest rank in Midland?

294
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:13,750
Utter nonsense...

295
00:19:14,170 --> 00:19:16,340
This is quite unexpected.

296
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,050
Indeed...

297
00:19:18,170 --> 00:19:19,670
This is wonderful!

298
00:19:21,010 --> 00:19:23,720
You will meet your end shortly...

299
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:27,100
Go on and revel in your
illusive glory while you still can.

300
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:35,860
It is about time, Mr. Foss.

301
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,320
What's wrong with you?

302
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:41,320
You look really pale...

303
00:19:42,910 --> 00:19:44,700
This is unlike you.

304
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:46,780
Is it because you are afraid of...

305
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:49,700
N-No, of course I'm not...

306
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:52,080
Please pull yourself together, Minister Foss.

307
00:20:22,530 --> 00:20:23,610
Please, sir.

308
00:20:24,950 --> 00:20:26,950
Certainly, thank you.

309
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:44,510
Now, we should toast
the celebration of our young heroes...

310
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:49,350
...and of course,
the future prosperity of Midland.

311
00:20:49,350 --> 00:20:51,600
Excuse me, let me pass please.

312
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:53,100
Raise your glass!

313
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:55,770
Raise your glass!

314
00:20:56,310 --> 00:20:57,360
Cheers!

315
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:01,440
Please, make way.

316
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,070
Griffith...

317
00:21:41,070 --> 00:21:43,110
Griffith!

318
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

319
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

320
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

321
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

322
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

323
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

324
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

325
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

326
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

327
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

328
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

